---
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="About"
	description="About Michael Wilson"
	pubDate={new Date('August 08 2026')}
>
	<p>
		I'm a web developer who got into tech late but has always been interested in how things work. 
		I enjoy tinkering with hardware, experimenting with software, and documenting what I learn along the way.
	</p>

	<h2>What I work with</h2>
	<p>
		I've spent time with old laptops and cameras, learning Linux, setting up home servers, 
		and generally exploring what older or unconventional hardware can still do.
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>Photography:</strong> Astrophotography with old Canon DSLRs, automation with gphoto2 and shell scripts</li>
		<li><strong>Linux:</strong> Running it on vintage ThinkPads, setting up systems from scratch, playing with proxmox</li>
		<li><strong>Hardware:</strong> Arduino, ESP32, Raspberry Pi, NAS setups, and other single-board projects</li>
		<li><strong>Home automation:</strong> Home Assistant, self-hosting services, network automation</li>
		<li><strong>Web development:</strong> Building things with modern web tools and thinking about performance</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>This site</h2>
	<p>
		It's built with <a href="https://astro.build">Astro</a>, a modern static site generator. 
		The aesthetic is intentionally minimal—just content, good typography, and plenty of whitespace. 
		No massive hero images or dark patterns. If you're interested in the code, 
		it's <a href="https://github.com/hobbitronics/astro">on GitHub</a>.
	</p>

	<h2>Get in touch</h2>
	<p>
		You can find my projects and code on <a href="https://github.com/hobbitronics">GitHub</a>. 
		Feel free to open an issue or send a message if something interests you.
	</p>
</Layout>
